V65 REVIEW PROPOSAL — NOT EXECUTABLE

Target: sales.POS_PostInvoice

Authoritative contract:
- @ItemsJson.UnitPrice is the customer-facing selling amount.
- The procedure joins each ProductId to master.Products within @TenantId.
- GstPricingType is never trusted from JSON.
- EXCLUSIVE keeps the existing taxable-basis calculation.
- INCLUSIVE treats the discounted gross amount as the line payable, extracts
  taxable amount = gross / (1 + GSTPercentage / 100), and stores the extracted
  GST without adding it to the line total.
- Invoice GrandTotal adds only additional GST from EXCLUSIVE lines.
- Invoice TaxAmount includes both extracted INCLUSIVE GST and additional
  EXCLUSIVE GST.

Required guarded changes to the existing procedure:

```diff
- @Tax DECIMAL(18,2)=0
+ @Tax DECIMAL(18,2)=0,@AdditionalTax DECIMAL(18,2)=0

- @Tax=SUM(((Quantity*UnitPrice)-Discount)*TaxPercentage/100)
- @Grand=ROUND(@Subtotal-@ItemDiscount-@BillDiscount+@Tax+@DeliveryCharge+@RoundOff,2)
+ @Tax=SUM(CASE WHEN p.GstPricingType=N'INCLUSIVE'
+   THEN ROUND(DiscountedGross*TaxPercentage/(100+TaxPercentage),2)
+   ELSE ROUND(DiscountedGross*TaxPercentage/100,2) END),
+ @AdditionalTax=SUM(CASE WHEN p.GstPricingType=N'INCLUSIVE' THEN 0
+   ELSE ROUND(DiscountedGross*TaxPercentage/100,2) END)
+ @Grand=ROUND(@Subtotal-@ItemDiscount-@BillDiscount+@AdditionalTax+
+   @DeliveryCharge+@RoundOff,2)

- cursor reads JSON items only
+ cursor joins master.Products by ProductId and reads persisted GstPricingType

- taxable=discounted gross; tax=taxable*rate/100; line=taxable+tax
+ INCLUSIVE: taxable=round(discounted gross/(1+rate/100),2),
+ tax=round(discounted gross-taxable,2), line=discounted gross
+ EXCLUSIVE: retain existing taxable/tax/line calculation
```

V65 must fail if the expected old procedure text/signature is absent, use
CREATE OR ALTER only after the exact replacement has been reviewed, and be
tested in WhatsBizERP_PosGstIntegrationTest before QA/PROD consideration.
